# P1: `/provider` mid-session keeps the conversation, and the next request
# carries the earlier turn in the new provider's shape. fx goes vercel ->
# codex (a seeded subscription sign-in, the Codex endpoints on the fake's own
# port, so nothing reaches a browser or the network); xfx goes gateway ->
# llmux (the fake's port is the daemon). The first turn reads a file under a
# call id no Anthropic `tool_use` takes (`functions.read:0`, upstream's own
# vector, tool_call_ids.zig:139). Then a resume, and one more turn. The
# context meter and the session title are on, to show what the footer keeps.
fx: seed provider-carry-fx.json
xfx: seed provider-carry-xfx.json
fx: homefile .fx/chatgpt-auth.json provider-carry-chatgpt-auth.json
fx: env FX_E2E_OPENAI_CODEX_MODELS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:@PORT@/codex/models FX_E2E_OPENAI_CODEX_RESPONSES_URL=http://127.0.0.1:@PORT@/codex/responses
nomodel
gateway provider-carry-turns.json
work provider-carry-ws
wait 6
snap start
type read the notes and tell me what they say
key Enter
wait 15
snap turn1
type /provider
key Enter
wait 4
snap open
key Down
wait 1
key Enter
wait 10
snap switched
home switched
type what day was it again?
key Enter
wait 15
snap turn2
keep
type /quit
key Enter
wait 4
snap quit
fx: relaunch --resume-last
xfx: relaunch --resume last
wait 10
snap resumed
type and after the resume?
key Enter
wait 15
snap turn3
home end
gwlog
type /quit
key Enter
wait 3
